/-!
# The symmetric-seven branch of Lemma 14.4.11

The conditional source theorem chooses Sylow-compatible seven-point
coordinates and constructs the literal pointwise-stabilizer residuals. It
proves the complete three-member X-family, identifies Wᵍ* with the three
pair swaps, and proves the exact two-member Y-family and its S₃ × S₃ overlap
quotient. The actual conjugate-pair action and precise earlier local geometry
remain explicit; the module also supplies the partner used by 14.4.13.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
Lemma 14.4.11, printed p.1011.
-/
